WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.380
We want the agent to total Northwind’s
charges.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.460
A human defines this blueprint: make the
billing package

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.620
available, deny by default, and allow a
charge lookup only

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.020
for the customer supplied by the
application.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.226
Here, that is Northwind.

00:00:17.533 --> 00:00:21.133
The agent writes this program in
Submilli’s curated subset

00:00:21.213 --> 00:00:22.093
of TypeScript.

00:00:22.573 --> 00:00:26.093
It imports the billing package, reads
Northwind’s charges,

00:00:26.173 --> 00:00:27.373
and totals the amounts.

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:29.853
The runtime runs the code;

00:00:29.933 --> 00:00:31.979
the package exposes the lookup.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.980
Submilli first checks the code against its
supported language,

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.020
standard APIs, and the packages selected
by the blueprint.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.820
Unknown APIs and unavailable imports fail
here, before execution.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.462
Valid code still needs permission for
protected operations.

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:55.847
Before reading charges, the package
explicitly asks Submilli

00:00:55.927 --> 00:00:58.407
to check the operation and customer ID.

00:00:59.047 --> 00:01:00.887
The runtime applies the blueprint.

00:01:01.447 --> 00:01:04.247
Northwind matches, so the lookup proceeds.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:07.414
This example uses a local billing ledger.

00:01:08.733 --> 00:01:11.293
Change only the customer to Initech.

00:01:11.853 --> 00:01:14.213
The code still passes language checking.

00:01:14.493 --> 00:01:18.093
The permission check now denies the
lookup: Initech does

00:01:18.173 --> 00:01:21.168
not match the application’s Northwind
context.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.340
Northwind’s program returns two charges,
totaling six thousand

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.100
one hundred and fifty cents.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.420
The language limits the code.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.180
The blueprint limits permitted operations
and arguments.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.420
People define the rules;

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.853
Submilli enforces the checks.
